[2026-02-04T17:27:24.682Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DoNNU8fMVxhhkm1TbAyaKd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"DOGE federal workforce reduction 270000 employees severance costs 2025 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Federal agencies are rehiring workers and spending more after DOGE's push to cut\",\"url\":\"https://www.npr.org/2025/10/01/nx-s1-5558298/doge-fiscal-year-savings-budget-rehired-government-shutdown\"},{\"title\":\"2025 United States federal mass layoffs - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_United_States_federal_mass_layoffs\"},{\"title\":\"Federal agencies are rehiring workers and spending more after DOGE’s push to cut - OPB\",\"url\":\"https://www.opb.org/article/2025/10/01/doge-cuts-to-federal-government-staffing-and-spending-are-being-undone/\"},{\"title\":\"Elon Musk's DOGE tally: The federal workforce is down while government spending is up\",\"url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/elon-musks-doge-tally-the-federal-workforce-is-down-while-government-spending-is-up-192850019.html\"},{\"title\":\"DOGE Layoffs: 5 Legal Options for Federal Employees Right Now | The Law Office of Justin Schnitzer\",\"url\":\"https://www.fedelaw.com/doge-layoffs/\"},{\"title\":\"New Analysis Shows DOGE Didn’t Cut Spending, But Delivered Historic Workforce Shrink Instead\",\"url\":\"https://allwork.space/2025/12/new-analysis-shows-doge-didnt-cut-spending-but-delivered-historic-workforce-shrink-instead/\"},{\"title\":\"DOGE Produced the Largest Peacetime Workforce Cut on Record, but Spending Kept Rising | Cato at Liberty Blog\",\"url\":\"https://www.cato.org/blog/doge-produced-largest-peacetime-workforce-cut-record-spending-kept-rising-0\"},{\"title\":\"How DOGE's Severance Plan May Affect Federal Employees\",\"url\":\"https://www.khflaw.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Law360-How-DOGEs-Severance-Plan-May-Affect-Federal-Employees.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Project 2025 wanted to hobble the federal workforce. DOGE has hastily done that, and more - Government Executive\",\"url\":\"https://www.govexec.com/transition/2025/04/project-2025-wanted-hobble-federal-workforce-doge-has-hastily-done-and-more/404390/\"},{\"title\":\"Cuts and Consolidation: Trump’s Federal Reset in 2025\",\"url\":\"https://meritalk.com/articles/cuts-and-consolidation-trumps-federal-reset-in-2025/\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found regarding DOGE's federal workforce reduction and severance costs:\n\n## Workforce Reduction Numbers\n\nDOGE has eliminated over 279,000 federal jobs across 27 agencies since January 2025, which is very close to the 270,000 figure in your query. More specifically, federal civilian employment fell by about 271,000 workers from January to November 2025, a roughly 9% decline in less than a year. Nearly 60% of the reduction occurred in October, driven largely by a one-time civil service buyout.\n\n## Severance Costs\n\nRegarding severance, most DOGE federal layoffs don't include severance pay. Federal workers may receive payment for unused annual leave but not for sick leave. This suggests that while significant workforce reductions occurred, the severance costs were minimal compared to what they might have been if typical severance packages were provided.\n\n## Timeline and Impact\n\nBy mid-February, about 75,000 federal workers accepted a \"deferred-resignation\" deal, and the sharp October drop of over 150,000 was driven by the federal civil service buyout offer rather than normal attrition. Despite these massive workforce reductions, the federal government spent $7.6 trillion in the first 11 months of 2025, exceeding spending levels from prior years, and there was no clear break in the spending trend tied to DOGE's launch.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"14046daa-6c10-475f-8534-6f3da0f72b30","tool_use_result":{"query":"DOGE federal workforce reduction 270000 employees severance costs 2025 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01AJrjEstBDYUKew7XvN67op","content":[{"title":"Federal agencies are rehiring workers and spending more after DOGE's push to cut","url":"https://www.npr.org/2025/10/01/nx-s1-5558298/doge-fiscal-year-savings-budget-rehired-government-shutdown"},{"title":"2025 United States federal mass layoffs - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_United_States_federal_mass_layoffs"},{"title":"Federal agencies are rehiring workers and spending more after DOGE’s push to cut - OPB","url":"https://www.opb.org/article/2025/10/01/doge-cuts-to-federal-government-staffing-and-spending-are-being-undone/"},{"title":"Elon Musk's DOGE tally: The federal workforce is down while government spending is up","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/elon-musks-doge-tally-the-federal-workforce-is-down-while-government-spending-is-up-192850019.html"},{"title":"DOGE Layoffs: 5 Legal Options for Federal Employees Right Now | The Law Office of Justin Schnitzer","url":"https://www.fedelaw.com/doge-layoffs/"},{"title":"New Analysis Shows DOGE Didn’t Cut Spending, But Delivered Historic Workforce Shrink Instead","url":"https://allwork.space/2025/12/new-analysis-shows-doge-didnt-cut-spending-but-delivered-historic-workforce-shrink-instead/"},{"title":"DOGE Produced the Largest Peacetime Workforce Cut on Record, but Spending Kept Rising | Cato at Liberty Blog","url":"https://www.cato.org/blog/doge-produced-largest-peacetime-workforce-cut-record-spending-kept-rising-0"},{"title":"How DOGE's Severance Plan May Affect Federal Employees","url":"https://www.khflaw.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Law360-How-DOGEs-Severance-Plan-May-Affect-Federal-Employees.pdf"},{"title":"Project 2025 wanted to hobble the federal workforce. DOGE has hastily done that, and more - Government Executive","url":"https://www.govexec.com/transition/2025/04/project-2025-wanted-hobble-federal-workforce-doge-has-hastily-done-and-more/404390/"},{"title":"Cuts and Consolidation: Trump’s Federal Reset in 2025","url":"https://meritalk.com/articles/cuts-and-consolidation-trumps-federal-reset-in-2025/"}]},"Based on the web search results, here's what I found regarding DOGE's federal workforce reduction and severance costs:\n\n## Workforce Reduction Numbers\n\nDOGE has eliminated over 279,000 federal jobs across 27 agencies since January 2025, which is very close to the 270,000 figure in your query. More specifically, federal civilian employment fell by about 271,000 workers from January to November 2025, a roughly 9% decline in less than a year. Nearly 60% of the reduction occurred in October, driven largely by a one-time civil service buyout.\n\n## Severance Costs\n\nRegarding severance, most DOGE federal layoffs don't include severance pay. Federal workers may receive payment for unused annual leave but not for sick leave. This suggests that while significant workforce reductions occurred, the severance costs were minimal compared to what they might have been if typical severance packages were provided.\n\n## Timeline and Impact\n\nBy mid-February, about 75,000 federal workers accepted a \"deferred-resignation\" deal, and the sharp October drop of over 150,000 was driven by the federal civil service buyout offer rather than normal attrition. Despite these massive workforce reductions, the federal government spent $7.6 trillion in the first 11 months of 2025, exceeding spending levels from prior years, and there was no clear break in the spending trend tied to DOGE's launch."],"durationSeconds":7.822364600000001}}
