[2026-02-04T17:27:39.523Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ts7PEJHtrWcXeivVVAS2vL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"federal spending 2025 year-over-year increase Treasury Department actual outlays\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Treasury Confirms Spending Up $142 Billion in 2025 | Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget\",\"url\":\"https://www.crfb.org/press-releases/treasury-confirms-spending-142-billion-2025\"},{\"title\":\"https://bipartisanpolicy.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/Budget-Deficit.jpg\",\"url\":\"https://bipartisanpolicy.org/report/deficit-tracker/\"},{\"title\":\"Monthly Budget Review: February 2025 | Congressional Budget Office\",\"url\":\"https://www.cbo.gov/publication/61196/html\"},{\"title\":\"Federal Spending | U.S. Treasury Fiscal Data\",\"url\":\"https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/americas-finance-guide/federal-spending/\"},{\"title\":\"Fiscal 2025 Deficit Was $1.8 Trillion, CBO Says | Tax Notes\",\"url\":\"https://www.taxnotes.com/research/federal/legislative-documents/congressional-budget-office-reports/fiscal-2025-deficit-was-1.8-trillion-cbo-says/7t8mc\"},{\"title\":\"OUTLAYS BY FUNCTION\",\"url\":\"https://www.fiscal.treasury.gov/files/reports-statements/combined-statement/cs2025/outlay.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Monthly Budget Review: September 2025\",\"url\":\"https://www.cbo.gov/system/files/2025-10/60306-MBR.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Monthly Budget Review: Summary for Fiscal Year 2025 | Congressional Budget Office\",\"url\":\"https://www.cbo.gov/publication/61307\"},{\"title\":\"MBR: Summary for Fiscal Year 2025\",\"url\":\"https://www.cbo.gov/system/files/2025-11/61307-MBR-FY25-final.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Tracking federal expenditures in real time - The Hamilton Project\",\"url\":\"https://www.hamiltonproject.org/data/tracking-federal-expenditures-in-real-time/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what the Treasury Department reports about federal spending in 2025 on a year-over-year basis:\n\n## Fiscal Year 2025 Total Outlays\n\nTotal outlays for the United States Government in fiscal year 2025 were $7,010.0 billion, an increase of 4.1 percent or $275.1 billion above the amount from fiscal year 2024.\n\n## Calendar Year 2025 (First Half)\n\nFor the calendar year comparison, the federal government has already spent $3.6 trillion from January to June of 2025 – up $142 billion from this same period last year.\n\n## Key Components of the Increase\n\nThe year-over-year increase in outlays was driven by several major areas:\n\n- Social Security outlays were $1,580.7 billion in fiscal year 2025, an increase of 8.2 percent or $119.8 billion above the prior fiscal year.\n\n- Medicare outlays were $996.7 billion in fiscal year 2025, an increase of 14.0 percent or $122.6 billion above the prior fiscal year.\n\n- Net Interest outlays were $970.4 billion in fiscal year 2025, an increase of 10.1 percent or $89.3 billion above the prior fiscal year.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"f7dc4f71-908f-415a-9e17-7ae626d9fbf5","tool_use_result":{"query":"federal spending 2025 year-over-year increase Treasury Department actual outlays","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01EMSJh9WMEKjwdhxsCYfABB","content":[{"title":"Treasury Confirms Spending Up $142 Billion in 2025 | Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget","url":"https://www.crfb.org/press-releases/treasury-confirms-spending-142-billion-2025"},{"title":"https://bipartisanpolicy.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/Budget-Deficit.jpg","url":"https://bipartisanpolicy.org/report/deficit-tracker/"},{"title":"Monthly Budget Review: February 2025 | Congressional Budget Office","url":"https://www.cbo.gov/publication/61196/html"},{"title":"Federal Spending | U.S. Treasury Fiscal Data","url":"https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/americas-finance-guide/federal-spending/"},{"title":"Fiscal 2025 Deficit Was $1.8 Trillion, CBO Says | Tax Notes","url":"https://www.taxnotes.com/research/federal/legislative-documents/congressional-budget-office-reports/fiscal-2025-deficit-was-1.8-trillion-cbo-says/7t8mc"},{"title":"OUTLAYS BY FUNCTION","url":"https://www.fiscal.treasury.gov/files/reports-statements/combined-statement/cs2025/outlay.pdf"},{"title":"Monthly Budget Review: September 2025","url":"https://www.cbo.gov/system/files/2025-10/60306-MBR.pdf"},{"title":"Monthly Budget Review: Summary for Fiscal Year 2025 | Congressional Budget Office","url":"https://www.cbo.gov/publication/61307"},{"title":"MBR: Summary for Fiscal Year 2025","url":"https://www.cbo.gov/system/files/2025-11/61307-MBR-FY25-final.pdf"},{"title":"Tracking federal expenditures in real time - The Hamilton Project","url":"https://www.hamiltonproject.org/data/tracking-federal-expenditures-in-real-time/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what the Treasury Department reports about federal spending in 2025 on a year-over-year basis:\n\n## Fiscal Year 2025 Total Outlays\n\nTotal outlays for the United States Government in fiscal year 2025 were $7,010.0 billion, an increase of 4.1 percent or $275.1 billion above the amount from fiscal year 2024.\n\n## Calendar Year 2025 (First Half)\n\nFor the calendar year comparison, the federal government has already spent $3.6 trillion from January to June of 2025 – up $142 billion from this same period last year.\n\n## Key Components of the Increase\n\nThe year-over-year increase in outlays was driven by several major areas:\n\n- Social Security outlays were $1,580.7 billion in fiscal year 2025, an increase of 8.2 percent or $119.8 billion above the prior fiscal year.\n\n- Medicare outlays were $996.7 billion in fiscal year 2025, an increase of 14.0 percent or $122.6 billion above the prior fiscal year.\n\n- Net Interest outlays were $970.4 billion in fiscal year 2025, an increase of 10.1 percent or $89.3 billion above the prior fiscal year."],"durationSeconds":6.559584900000002}}
