[2026-02-04T17:27:51.078Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JaU1BQZcdrZq78WYz6bp7v","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"DOGE savings fact check Wall Street Journal Fox News conservative analysis\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Has DOGE really saved the US government $180bn? | Elon Musk News | Al Jazeera\",\"url\":\"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/6/6/has-doge-really-saved-the-us-government-180bn\"},{\"title\":\"Department of Government Efficiency - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Department_of_Government_Efficiency\"},{\"title\":\"Trump and Musk public bickering raises more DOGE uncertainty\",\"url\":\"https://www.politifact.com/article/2025/jun/05/elon-musk-donald-trump-doge-cuts/\"},{\"title\":\"Fiscal watchdog calls for better spending transparency in new government spending report | Fox News\",\"url\":\"https://www.foxnews.com/politics/trumps-doge-savings-dwarfed-medicare-social-security-spending-watchdog-finds\"},{\"title\":\"How Much Has DOGE Really Saved? Here’s the Scorecard to Date\",\"url\":\"https://mishtalk.com/economics/how-much-has-doge-really-saved-heres-the-scorecard-to-date/\"},{\"title\":\"Fox ignores projected $500B IRS shortfall after celebrating meager US DOGE savings | Media Matters for America\",\"url\":\"https://www.mediamatters.org/fox-news/fox-ignores-projected-500b-irs-shortfall-after-celebrating-meager-us-doge-savings\"},{\"title\":\"A look at the misleading and incorrect claims on DOGE's 'wall of receipts' | PBS News\",\"url\":\"https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/a-look-at-the-misleading-and-incorrect-claims-on-doges-wall-of-receipts\"},{\"title\":\"DOGE: Department of Government Efficiency\",\"url\":\"https://doge.gov/savings\"},{\"title\":\"DOGE continues to say it's cutting costs, but savings are fraction of what's claimed, CBS News analysis finds - CBS News\",\"url\":\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/doge-claims-slashing-costs-cbs-news-analysis/\"},{\"title\":\"DOGE's savings page fixed old mistakes — and added new ones\",\"url\":\"https://www.npr.org/2025/03/01/nx-s1-5313853/doge-savings-receipts-musk-trump\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what fact-checkers and analysts have found regarding DOGE's savings claims:\n\n## Key Findings from Multiple Outlets\n\nAnalyses by PolitiFact, The Wall Street Journal, The New York Times and the conservative American Enterprise Institute showed that the tallies Musk provided were flawed.\n\n## Specific Errors and Discrepancies\n\nDOGE's initial reported savings was inaccurate due to counting contracts multiple times, listing contracts that have already been paid as savings, and misrepresenting potential savings based on contract limits rather than actual spending. For example, a USAID contract for $650 million was listed three times, a Social Security contract was listed as $232 million instead of $560,000, and an ICE contract was listed as $8 billion when it was actually $8 million.\n\n## Actual vs. Claimed Savings\n\nMultiple independent analyses have produced dramatically lower figures than DOGE's claims. NPR analysis found estimated savings of only about $2 billion — a fraction of what the receipts claimed or the higher, unverifiable claim of $55 billion overall. The Wall Street Journal analysis projects the actual savings could be closer to $2.6 billion over the next year if spending levels remained constant.\n\n## Conservative Analysis\n\nNat Malkus, an education policy specialist at the conservative American Enterprise Institute, said DOGE's cuts showed an \"appetite for recklessness,\" and its error- and exaggeration-filled wall of receipts provided \"ample grounds for skepticism\" about its accuracy.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"7a9173ad-fccd-4c48-a9a7-07ea2dc3eb4e","tool_use_result":{"query":"DOGE savings fact check Wall Street Journal Fox News conservative analysis","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019FHm4qoYoR8G942eonDQnr","content":[{"title":"Has DOGE really saved the US government $180bn? | Elon Musk News | Al Jazeera","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/6/6/has-doge-really-saved-the-us-government-180bn"},{"title":"Department of Government Efficiency - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Department_of_Government_Efficiency"},{"title":"Trump and Musk public bickering raises more DOGE uncertainty","url":"https://www.politifact.com/article/2025/jun/05/elon-musk-donald-trump-doge-cuts/"},{"title":"Fiscal watchdog calls for better spending transparency in new government spending report | Fox News","url":"https://www.foxnews.com/politics/trumps-doge-savings-dwarfed-medicare-social-security-spending-watchdog-finds"},{"title":"How Much Has DOGE Really Saved? Here’s the Scorecard to Date","url":"https://mishtalk.com/economics/how-much-has-doge-really-saved-heres-the-scorecard-to-date/"},{"title":"Fox ignores projected $500B IRS shortfall after celebrating meager US DOGE savings | Media Matters for America","url":"https://www.mediamatters.org/fox-news/fox-ignores-projected-500b-irs-shortfall-after-celebrating-meager-us-doge-savings"},{"title":"A look at the misleading and incorrect claims on DOGE's 'wall of receipts' | PBS News","url":"https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/a-look-at-the-misleading-and-incorrect-claims-on-doges-wall-of-receipts"},{"title":"DOGE: Department of Government Efficiency","url":"https://doge.gov/savings"},{"title":"DOGE continues to say it's cutting costs, but savings are fraction of what's claimed, CBS News analysis finds - CBS News","url":"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/doge-claims-slashing-costs-cbs-news-analysis/"},{"title":"DOGE's savings page fixed old mistakes — and added new ones","url":"https://www.npr.org/2025/03/01/nx-s1-5313853/doge-savings-receipts-musk-trump"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what fact-checkers and analysts have found regarding DOGE's savings claims:\n\n## Key Findings from Multiple Outlets\n\nAnalyses by PolitiFact, The Wall Street Journal, The New York Times and the conservative American Enterprise Institute showed that the tallies Musk provided were flawed.\n\n## Specific Errors and Discrepancies\n\nDOGE's initial reported savings was inaccurate due to counting contracts multiple times, listing contracts that have already been paid as savings, and misrepresenting potential savings based on contract limits rather than actual spending. For example, a USAID contract for $650 million was listed three times, a Social Security contract was listed as $232 million instead of $560,000, and an ICE contract was listed as $8 billion when it was actually $8 million.\n\n## Actual vs. Claimed Savings\n\nMultiple independent analyses have produced dramatically lower figures than DOGE's claims. NPR analysis found estimated savings of only about $2 billion — a fraction of what the receipts claimed or the higher, unverifiable claim of $55 billion overall. The Wall Street Journal analysis projects the actual savings could be closer to $2.6 billion over the next year if spending levels remained constant.\n\n## Conservative Analysis\n\nNat Malkus, an education policy specialist at the conservative American Enterprise Institute, said DOGE's cuts showed an \"appetite for recklessness,\" and its error- and exaggeration-filled wall of receipts provided \"ample grounds for skepticism\" about its accuracy."],"durationSeconds":7.909485500000002}}
