[2026-02-04T17:28:05.598Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019is3EHJmYRoBoEc8VwJSaA","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"DOGE $135 billion cost analysis Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget methodology\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"DOGE says it has saved $160 billion. Those cuts have cost taxpayers $135 billion, one analysis says. - CBS News\",\"url\":\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/doge-cuts-cost-135-billion-analysis-elon-musk-department-of-government-efficiency/\"},{\"title\":\"Department of Government Efficiency - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Department_of_Government_Efficiency\"},{\"title\":\"DOGE’s mass federal workforce cuts may cost taxpayers $135 billion this fiscal year alone | Fortune\",\"url\":\"https://fortune.com/article/doge-mass-federal-workforce-cuts-taxpayers-billions/\"},{\"title\":\"The first 100 days of DOGE: \\\"not successful by any means”\",\"url\":\"https://www.marketplace.org/story/2025/04/29/doges-costcutting-has-been-underwhelming-at-best\"},{\"title\":\"Did the DOGE Committee Deliver on Efficiency? A Deep Dive into New Texas Spending\",\"url\":\"https://www.texaspolicyresearch.com/did-the-doge-committee-deliver-on-efficiency-a-deep-dive-into-new-texas-spending/\"},{\"title\":\"Analysis: Scorecard: How Musk and DOGE could end up costing more than they save | CNN Politics\",\"url\":\"https://www.cnn.com/2025/05/30/politics/doge-musk-government-savings\"},{\"title\":\"Is Elon Musk’s DOGE task force exposing federal spending or putting lives at risk?\",\"url\":\"https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/doge/elon-musk-doge-task-force-federal-spending-rcna190963\"},{\"title\":\"DOGE released data about federal contract savings. It doesn’t add up : NPR\",\"url\":\"https://www.npr.org/2025/02/19/nx-s1-5302705/doge-overstates-savings-federal-contracts\"},{\"title\":\"Watchdog identifies $100B in potential government cost savings | FedScoop\",\"url\":\"https://fedscoop.com/gao-finds-100-billion-cost-savings-doge/\"},{\"title\":\"Full List of DOGE Spending Cuts, Findings as Trump Marks One Month Into Second Presidency - Newsweek\",\"url\":\"https://www.newsweek.com/doge-spending-cuts-findings-one-month-trump-administration-2034150\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding the $135 billion cost analysis:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nA nonpartisan research and advocacy group estimated that DOGE's actions will cost $135 billion this fiscal year. However, it's important to note that this analysis was conducted by the **Partnership for Public Service**, not the Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget.\n\n## Methodology\n\nThe analysis seeks to tally the costs associated with putting tens of thousands of federal employees on paid leave, re-hiring mistakenly fired workers and lost productivity. More specifically, PSP's estimate is based on the $270 billion in annual compensation costs for the federal workforce, calculating the impact of DOGE's actions, from paid leave to productivity hits.\n\nThis estimate did not include the costs of lawsuits or lower tax collections.\n\n## Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget Reference\n\nWhile the Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget was mentioned in relation to DOGE, the search results show that Maya MacGuineas, the president of the bipartisan nonprofit Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget, says she has some sympathy for what the DOGE team is trying to do. However, the $135 billion cost analysis appears to be specifically attributed to the Partnership for Public Service rather than the Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"428006fa-95b7-4ca6-825e-aa2f84110c9c","tool_use_result":{"query":"DOGE $135 billion cost analysis Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget methodology","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01CBtupiQ2j7wY8jag9vsBPC","content":[{"title":"DOGE says it has saved $160 billion. Those cuts have cost taxpayers $135 billion, one analysis says. - CBS News","url":"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/doge-cuts-cost-135-billion-analysis-elon-musk-department-of-government-efficiency/"},{"title":"Department of Government Efficiency - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Department_of_Government_Efficiency"},{"title":"DOGE’s mass federal workforce cuts may cost taxpayers $135 billion this fiscal year alone | Fortune","url":"https://fortune.com/article/doge-mass-federal-workforce-cuts-taxpayers-billions/"},{"title":"The first 100 days of DOGE: \"not successful by any means”","url":"https://www.marketplace.org/story/2025/04/29/doges-costcutting-has-been-underwhelming-at-best"},{"title":"Did the DOGE Committee Deliver on Efficiency? A Deep Dive into New Texas Spending","url":"https://www.texaspolicyresearch.com/did-the-doge-committee-deliver-on-efficiency-a-deep-dive-into-new-texas-spending/"},{"title":"Analysis: Scorecard: How Musk and DOGE could end up costing more than they save | CNN Politics","url":"https://www.cnn.com/2025/05/30/politics/doge-musk-government-savings"},{"title":"Is Elon Musk’s DOGE task force exposing federal spending or putting lives at risk?","url":"https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/doge/elon-musk-doge-task-force-federal-spending-rcna190963"},{"title":"DOGE released data about federal contract savings. It doesn’t add up : NPR","url":"https://www.npr.org/2025/02/19/nx-s1-5302705/doge-overstates-savings-federal-contracts"},{"title":"Watchdog identifies $100B in potential government cost savings | FedScoop","url":"https://fedscoop.com/gao-finds-100-billion-cost-savings-doge/"},{"title":"Full List of DOGE Spending Cuts, Findings as Trump Marks One Month Into Second Presidency - Newsweek","url":"https://www.newsweek.com/doge-spending-cuts-findings-one-month-trump-administration-2034150"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found regarding the $135 billion cost analysis:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nA nonpartisan research and advocacy group estimated that DOGE's actions will cost $135 billion this fiscal year. However, it's important to note that this analysis was conducted by the **Partnership for Public Service**, not the Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget.\n\n## Methodology\n\nThe analysis seeks to tally the costs associated with putting tens of thousands of federal employees on paid leave, re-hiring mistakenly fired workers and lost productivity. More specifically, PSP's estimate is based on the $270 billion in annual compensation costs for the federal workforce, calculating the impact of DOGE's actions, from paid leave to productivity hits.\n\nThis estimate did not include the costs of lawsuits or lower tax collections.\n\n## Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget Reference\n\nWhile the Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget was mentioned in relation to DOGE, the search results show that Maya MacGuineas, the president of the bipartisan nonprofit Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget, says she has some sympathy for what the DOGE team is trying to do. However, the $135 billion cost analysis appears to be specifically attributed to the Partnership for Public Service rather than the Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget."],"durationSeconds":6.310584700000007}}
