[2026-02-04T17:28:17.320Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019UeXpK7cJ79mBZU9omUjaQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Cato Institute DOGE spending analysis federal workforce cuts fiscal impact\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"DOGE Produced the Largest Peacetime Workforce Cut on Record, but Spending Kept Rising | Cato at Liberty Blog\",\"url\":\"https://www.cato.org/blog/doge-produced-largest-peacetime-workforce-cut-record-spending-kept-rising-0\"},{\"title\":\"New Analysis Shows DOGE Didn’t Cut Spending, But Delivered Historic Workforce Shrink Instead\",\"url\":\"https://allwork.space/2025/12/new-analysis-shows-doge-didnt-cut-spending-but-delivered-historic-workforce-shrink-instead/\"},{\"title\":\"Elon Musk's DOGE tally: The federal workforce is down while government spending is up\",\"url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/elon-musks-doge-tally-the-federal-workforce-is-down-while-government-spending-is-up-192850019.html\"},{\"title\":\"DOGE Took a Chainsaw to the Federal Workforce\",\"url\":\"https://www.alexnowrasteh.com/p/doge-set-a-record-for-the-largest\"},{\"title\":\"DOGE did not reduce overall spending, but boasts largest peacetime workforce reduction on record - Washington Times\",\"url\":\"https://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2025/dec/19/doge-reduce-overall-spending-boasts-largest-peacetime-workforce/\"},{\"title\":\"DOGE cut jobs, but did it cut government spending? - WTOP News\",\"url\":\"https://wtop.com/government/2025/12/doge-cut-jobs-but-did-it-cut-government-spending/\"},{\"title\":\"Report: Federal Workforce Down Nine Percent in 2025, but Spending Continued to Grow - The New American\",\"url\":\"https://thenewamerican.com/us/politics/report-federal-workforce-down-nine-percent-in-2025-but-spending-continued-to-grow/\"},{\"title\":\"Cato's Recommendations To DOGE For Slashing Federal Employee Pay, Benefits | FedSmith.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.fedsmith.com/2024/12/20/catos-recommendations-to-doge-for-slashing-federal-employee-pay-benefits/\"},{\"title\":\"DOGE cuts to federal government staffing and spending ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.npr.org/2025/10/01/nx-s1-5558298/doge-fiscal-year-savings-budget-rehired-government-shutdown\"},{\"title\":\"Elon Musk’s DOGE Cuts Fail to Stop US Spending From Hitting Record - Newsweek\",\"url\":\"https://www.newsweek.com/elon-musks-doge-cuts-fail-stop-us-federal-spending-hitting-new-record-2043799\"}]\n\nBased on the Cato Institute analysis, here are the key findings on DOGE's spending and federal workforce impact:\n\n## Federal Spending Impact\n\nDOGE fell short of its core goal to reduce federal spending, but it delivered one of the fastest peacetime reductions in the federal workforce on record. Federal government spent $7.6 trillion in the first 11 months of 2025, exceeding spending levels from prior years and closely tracking Congressional Budget Office projections.\n\nMost federal spending is driven by entitlement programs, which DOGE lacked authority to change. As a result, outlays continued largely unchanged despite the initiative's stated goals.\n\n## Workforce Reductions\n\nFederal civilian employment fell by about 271,000 workers from January to November 2025, a roughly 9% decline in less than a year. Nearly 60% of the reduction occurred in October, driven largely by a one-time civil service buyout.\n\n## Fiscal Impact of Workforce Cuts\n\nDespite the massive workforce reduction, the fiscal savings were limited. According to Cato's report to the DOGE Commission last year, a 10 percent cut in the federal workforce would only save about $40 billion annually. The 3.8 million federal defense and nondefense employees, excluding postal workers, account for around 8 percent of total spending, which explains why workforce cuts had minimal impact on overall spending.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"6aeeddf9-14dc-4746-9903-8daf0cbab398","tool_use_result":{"query":"Cato Institute DOGE spending analysis federal workforce cuts fiscal impact","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01CPyEGU23CUtkgPadE16X4R","content":[{"title":"DOGE Produced the Largest Peacetime Workforce Cut on Record, but Spending Kept Rising | Cato at Liberty Blog","url":"https://www.cato.org/blog/doge-produced-largest-peacetime-workforce-cut-record-spending-kept-rising-0"},{"title":"New Analysis Shows DOGE Didn’t Cut Spending, But Delivered Historic Workforce Shrink Instead","url":"https://allwork.space/2025/12/new-analysis-shows-doge-didnt-cut-spending-but-delivered-historic-workforce-shrink-instead/"},{"title":"Elon Musk's DOGE tally: The federal workforce is down while government spending is up","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/elon-musks-doge-tally-the-federal-workforce-is-down-while-government-spending-is-up-192850019.html"},{"title":"DOGE Took a Chainsaw to the Federal Workforce","url":"https://www.alexnowrasteh.com/p/doge-set-a-record-for-the-largest"},{"title":"DOGE did not reduce overall spending, but boasts largest peacetime workforce reduction on record - Washington Times","url":"https://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2025/dec/19/doge-reduce-overall-spending-boasts-largest-peacetime-workforce/"},{"title":"DOGE cut jobs, but did it cut government spending? - WTOP News","url":"https://wtop.com/government/2025/12/doge-cut-jobs-but-did-it-cut-government-spending/"},{"title":"Report: Federal Workforce Down Nine Percent in 2025, but Spending Continued to Grow - The New American","url":"https://thenewamerican.com/us/politics/report-federal-workforce-down-nine-percent-in-2025-but-spending-continued-to-grow/"},{"title":"Cato's Recommendations To DOGE For Slashing Federal Employee Pay, Benefits | FedSmith.com","url":"https://www.fedsmith.com/2024/12/20/catos-recommendations-to-doge-for-slashing-federal-employee-pay-benefits/"},{"title":"DOGE cuts to federal government staffing and spending ...","url":"https://www.npr.org/2025/10/01/nx-s1-5558298/doge-fiscal-year-savings-budget-rehired-government-shutdown"},{"title":"Elon Musk’s DOGE Cuts Fail to Stop US Spending From Hitting Record - Newsweek","url":"https://www.newsweek.com/elon-musks-doge-cuts-fail-stop-us-federal-spending-hitting-new-record-2043799"}]},"Based on the Cato Institute analysis, here are the key findings on DOGE's spending and federal workforce impact:\n\n## Federal Spending Impact\n\nDOGE fell short of its core goal to reduce federal spending, but it delivered one of the fastest peacetime reductions in the federal workforce on record. Federal government spent $7.6 trillion in the first 11 months of 2025, exceeding spending levels from prior years and closely tracking Congressional Budget Office projections.\n\nMost federal spending is driven by entitlement programs, which DOGE lacked authority to change. As a result, outlays continued largely unchanged despite the initiative's stated goals.\n\n## Workforce Reductions\n\nFederal civilian employment fell by about 271,000 workers from January to November 2025, a roughly 9% decline in less than a year. Nearly 60% of the reduction occurred in October, driven largely by a one-time civil service buyout.\n\n## Fiscal Impact of Workforce Cuts\n\nDespite the massive workforce reduction, the fiscal savings were limited. According to Cato's report to the DOGE Commission last year, a 10 percent cut in the federal workforce would only save about $40 billion annually. The 3.8 million federal defense and nondefense employees, excluding postal workers, account for around 8 percent of total spending, which explains why workforce cuts had minimal impact on overall spending."],"durationSeconds":8.3202883}}
